e the mystery sentence. Move each word to place it in the correct order.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}]}], "id": 9, "stimuli_ids": []}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "RSLT", "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0}, {"id": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "id": 10, "stimuli_ids": []}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "DWS", "questions": [{"responses": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn10le03ob05re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " You want to insist on something. Prepare a dialogue.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le03ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le03ob05re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn10le03ob05re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn10le03ob05re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Secretary</span>: Welcome to BFP. How can I help you?\n<Br/><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Hello, I would like to see Mr. Brody, please.\n<Br/><span class=\"strong\">Secretary</span>: Your name, please?\n<Br/><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Adam Bari.\n<Br/><span class=\"strong\">Secretary</span>: Do you have an appointment?\n<Br/><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: No, actually.\n<Br/><span class=\"strong\">Secretary</span>: I'm sorry, but Mr. Brody is not available. Could I ask what is the nature of your visit?\n<Br/><span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I am interested in employment. I have a friend, Kristi Lenard, who was just offered a job as editorial assistant. She has informed me there was another position available.\n<Br/> <span class=\"strong\">Secretary</span>: You need to send your r\u00e9sum\u00e9 by e-mail.", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn10le03ob05re2img06.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Yes, I've already done that. The problem is that I couldn't find the job advertised yesterday. I suspect you have taken down the job posting from the website. This makes me nervous, because I haven't been called in for an interview yet.\n<Br/> <span class=\"strong\">Secretary</span>: You needn't worry. If Mr. Brody has received your r\u00e9sum\u00e9, he will consider it alongside the other candidates, in all fairness. I think you have done everything you can.\n<Br/> <span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>:  I believe my friend has talked to Mr. Brody about me. I would just like introduce myself quickly.\n<Br/> <span class=\"strong\">Secretary</span>:  I'm sorry, but that's impossible. You mustn't insist further. Mr. Brody is a very busy man.", "id": 2, "time": "30000"}, {"image": "engenn10le03ob05re2img07.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I hope that I have not annoyed you.  Please, believe me, Mr. Brody knows who I am and has expressed an interest in meeting me. I'm sorry to insist, but I really must see Mr. Brody. He will understand. He will agree to meet me.\n<Br/> <span class=\"strong\">Secretary</span>: This is a most unusual situation.\n<Br/> <span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Yes, I understand that it appears that way.\n<Br/> <span class=\"strong\">Secretary</span>:  Since you are so insistent, I will ask Mr. Brody if he is willing to meet you.\n<Br/> <span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Oh, thank you!", "id": 3, "time": "65000"}]}}], "_data": []}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Looking for a Job", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Getting  a Second Chance", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Discuss factual and abstract information about common everyday or job related topics in both work and social contexts appropriate for the interlocutor.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.er", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "in all fairness", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be fair and just towards other people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If Mr. Brody has received your r\u00e9sum\u00e9, he will consider it alongside the other candidates, in all fairness.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you meet a receptionist at a company.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take down", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to remove", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I suspect you have taken down the job posting from the website.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "the nature of your visit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the reason you are here", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Could I ask what is the nature of your visit?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to insist", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to demand or ask repetitively", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You mustn't insist any further. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "insistent", "type": "name"}, {"content": "describes a person who does not let go of an idea when talking to other people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Since you are so insistent, I will ask Mr. Brody if he is willing to meet you. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Using the Present Perfect Tense to Refer to Past Actions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense to talk about a past event or action that is connected to the present in some way.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense when you don't know when the event happened, or when that information is not important. You refer to an unspecified time in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:  </br></br><span class=\"italic\">She has informed me there was another position available. </span></br></br>The structure of the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">subject</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">has/have</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">past participle</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I/They/We/You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"been\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It/He/She\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"has\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"worked\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I suspect you have taken down the job posting from the website.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I believe my friend has talked to Mr. Brody about me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I hope that I have not annoyed you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are some verbs which express a previous thought before an action. These verbs can be used before the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect </span> tense to refer to a past action. E.g. <span class=\"italic\">assume</span>, <span class=\"italic\">believe</span>, <span class=\"italic\">expect</span>, <span class=\"italic\">guess</span>, <span class=\"italic\">hope</span>, <span class=\"italic\">imagine</span>, <span class=\"italic\">presume</span>, <span class=\"italic\">suppose</span>, <span class=\"italic\">suspect</span> and <span class=\"italic\">think</span>.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Modals Expressing Necessity: Need and Must", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you want to express necessity or when things are not necessary, you use modals.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The modal <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">need</span> </span>refers to necessity, when something is an obligation.  </br></br> For example:  </br></br><span class=\"italic\"> You <span class=\"strong\">need </span>to send your r\u00e9sum\u00e9 by e-mail.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">need not</span></span>  (<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">needn't</span></span>) when you want to refer to something that is not necessary. Because it is rather formal sounding, you use it mainly in workplace settings or in writing. In conversation, you most often use <span class=\"italic\">have to</span> or <span class=\"italic\">don't have to</span>. </br></br> For example:  </br></br><span class=\"italic\">You<span class=\"strong\"> needn't </span>worry. If Mr. Brody has received your  r\u00e9sum\u00e9, he will consider it alongside the other candidates.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The modal <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">must</span></span> refers to strong necessity, when something is absolutely necessary.   </br></br>For example:  </br></br><span class=\"italic\">I'm sorry to insist, but I really <span class=\"strong\">must </span>see Mr. Brody. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">  must not</span></span>  (<span class=\"italic\">mustn't</span>) to talk about things that are prohibited. This is very strong language. </br></br> For example:</br></br><span class=\"italic\">  You <span class=\"strong\"> mustn't</span>  insist any further.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'm sorry, but I must ask you to leave.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You mustn't stay in the office area after we close for the day.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a dialogue insisting on something.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express what is necessary.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I refuse and then accept a demand.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think of a situation in which you need to insist on something. It could be at work, at a store, at a hospital, etc.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a dialogue of 120 - 150 words. One person insists on something. The other person starts to refuse, but ends by accepting.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use appropriate vocabulary, like in <span class=\"italic\">all fairness </span>and you <span class=\"italic\">mustn't insist</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice your dialogue with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Change roles.", "type": "text"}]}]}